// DEV-856 fix overlay. NOT generated by Speakeasy; hand-maintained.
//
// The Speakeasy-generated RefreshFromShared*Response functions populate the
// typed per-variant nested config (r.Webhook.Config, r.Arize.Config, ...) but
// never repopulate the flat `config` map (r.Config) that users actually write
// in their HCL. As a result, after Create/Update the state's `config` comes
// from refreshPlan (the plan), not from the API, and Read never round-trips
// it at all. Any API-side normalization of the config map then shows up as a
// perpetual diff.
//
// This file provides refreshFlatConfigFromResponse, which identifies the
// active oneOf variant in an API response and serializes its typed Config
// struct back into the flat map[string]jsontypes.Normalized form stored in
// Terraform state. It is wired into Create/Update/Read after the generated
// RefreshFromShared* calls.
//
// To make this survive the next Speakeasy regen, the same logic needs to be
// expressed via the generator's terraform-entities-overlay.yaml as a
// post-read/refresh hook, or upstreamed into Speakeasy's Terraform generator
// so flat additionalProperties maps hoisted from oneOf variants are refreshed
// from the active variant. Tracked as DEV-856 follow-up.

package provider

import (
	"encoding/json"
	"fmt"

	"github.com/OpenRouterTeam/terraform-provider-openrouter/internal/sdk/models/shared"
	"github.com/hashicorp/terraform-plugin-framework-jsontypes/jsontypes"
	"github.com/hashicorp/terraform-plugin-framework/diag"
)

// refreshFlatConfigFromCreateResponse rebuilds the flat `config` state map
